<section>
  <exercises>
    <heading level="1">Section 9.2 Exercises</heading>
    <heading level="1">Practice Makes Perfect</heading>
    <paragraph>Complete the Square of a Binomial Expression</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, complete the square to make a perfect square trinomial. Then write the result as a binomial squared.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="71" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$m^{2} - 24m$$ ⓑ $$x^{2} - 11x$$ ⓒ $$p^{2} - \frac{1}{3}p$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$(m-12)2(m-12)2$$ ⓑ $$(x-112)2(x-112)2$$ ⓒ $$(p-16)2(p-16)2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="72" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$n^{2} - 16n$$ ⓑ $$y^{2} + 15y$$ ⓒ $$q^{2} + \frac{3}{4}q$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="73" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$p^{2} - 22p$$ ⓑ $$y^{2} + 5y$$ ⓒ $$m^{2} + \frac{2}{5}m$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$(p-11)2(p-11)2$$ ⓑ $$(y+52)2(y+52)2$$ ⓒ $$(m+15)2(m+15)2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="74" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$q^{2} - 6q$$ ⓑ $$x^{2} - 7x$$ ⓒ $$n^{2} - \frac{2}{3}n$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
